Alaska Manager Code of Conduct
As Licensed Managers or Trainees, individuals understand their obligation to conduct all aspects of their responsibilities with honesty and integrity and always to present a positive image of the Alaska Business Enterprise Program and blind people in general. Accordingly, all Vending Facility Managers and new Trainees must agree to the following:
Deal honestly with all customers, employees, suppliers, property management officials, SLA staff, and anyone else with whom they have contact in my capacity with BEP;
Treat with dignity and respect customers, employees, suppliers, property management officials, SLA staff, and others with whom they have contact in their capacity with BEP;
Create a safe workplace, free of sexual harassment or any manner of sexual misconduct, and is not considered by employees or others to be a hostile environment;
Ensure an alcohol and drug-free environment and never be at the facility while intoxicated or under the influence of illegal drugs;
Embrace diversity and promote full participation while refraining from demeaning, derogatory, or discriminatory language;

